Subject: unix: yield with sched_yield, which is not a cancellation point
Fixes: E1 - _mi_prim_thread_yield called sleep(0), a POSIX cancellation point, inside busy-waits on mi_free and thread-exit paths
Upstream: to report

POSIX (Issue 8, XSH 2.9.5.2) requires sleep() to be a cancellation point;
sched_yield() is in neither list. v3.6.1's _mi_prim_thread_yield, used in
the busy-waits of src/arena/bitmap-chunk.c (122-125, reached from mi_free
when a page is being unabandoned concurrently), src/heap/theap.c (438 and
470, the latter inside mi_lock(&tld->theaps_lock) at thread exit) and the
fallback lock of include/mimalloc/atomic.h (550), called sleep(0). A
deferred cancellation acted on there either left a page owned and abandoned
for ever or a lock held, and with -fno-exceptions the forced unwind passed
through mimalloc's frames (audit E1, E2, E5). sched_yield() gives the same
yield without a cancellation point. sleep is no longer used in this file,
so the comment on the unistd.h include is updated and sched.h is included.
STXlib also blocks cancellation around its allocator calls
(src/state/allocator.cpp); this patch covers the paths that do not go
through them, such as thread exit.

--- a/src/prim/unix/prim.c
+++ b/src/prim/unix/prim.c
@@ -29,7 +29,8 @@
 #include "mimalloc/heap/process.h"
 
 #include <sys/mman.h>  // mmap
-#include <unistd.h>    // sysconf, sleep
+#include <unistd.h>    // sysconf
+#include <sched.h>     // sched_yield
 #include <fcntl.h>     // open, close, read, access
 #include <stdlib.h>    // getenv, arc4random_buf
 
@@ -1148,7 +1149,10 @@
 }
 
 void _mi_prim_thread_yield(void) {
-  sleep(0);
+  // sched_yield, not sleep(0): sleep is a POSIX cancellation point and this yield sits
+  // in busy-waits reached from mi_free (bitmap-chunk.c) and thread exit (theap.c, inside
+  // the tld's theaps_lock), where a cancellation would leave a page claimed or a lock held.
+  sched_yield();
 }
 
 bool _mi_prim_process_is_killed(void) {
